<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiang Qing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1991</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jiang Qing was a Chinese actress and politician, the fourth wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a> she led radical attacks on the arts and party officials and became the most prominent member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gang-of-four">Gang of Four</a>. Arrested in October 1976, a month after Mao's death, she was tried in 1980–81 and sentenced to death, commuted to life imprisonment; she died in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiang-qing.jpg" alt="Jiang Qing" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jiang_Qing_1976.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
